To get the Total Amount and Total Record Count within your getOrGenerateLhoSummary call, you need to calculate these values during the aggregation loop and change your return type from a simple Map to a structured Response Object.
As a Lead, I recommend creating a specific DTO for this summary response. This ensures your API remains predictable and easy for the frontend to consume.
1. Create a Summary Response DTO
This DTO will wrap your circle-wise data along with the metadata.
package com.tcs.fincore.CommonMasterService.dto;

import lombok.Builder;
import lombok.Data;
import java.math.BigDecimal;
import java.util.Map;

@Data
@Builder
public class LhoSummaryResponseDto {
    private BigDecimal totalAmount;
    private int totalRecordCount;
    private Map<String, BigDecimal> circleWiseDetails;
}

2. Update the Service Logic
You need to calculate the sum and the count while iterating through the aggregatedData.
@Override
@Transactional
public Object getOrGenerateLhoSummary(Long id) {
    log.info("Processing LHO Summary request for ID: {}", id);

    // --- STEP 1: CHECK CACHE ---
    Optional<LhoTransferSummary> cached = lhoSummaryRepository.findById(id);
    if (cached.isPresent()) {
        try {
            // Updated to use the new DTO structure
            return objectMapper.readValue(cached.get().getPayload(), LhoSummaryResponseDto.class);
        } catch (Exception e) {
            log.error("Error parsing cached summary JSON: {}", e.getMessage());
            return cached.get().getPayload();
        }
    }

    // --- STEP 2: AGGREGATE ---
    List<Object[]> aggregatedData = plTransferRepository.getAggregatedSummary();
    if (aggregatedData.isEmpty()) return Collections.emptyMap();

    Map<String, BigDecimal> summaryMap = new HashMap<>();
    BigDecimal totalAmount = BigDecimal.ZERO;

    for (Object[] row : aggregatedData) {
        String branchCode = String.valueOf(row[0]);
        BigDecimal totalPL = (row[1] != null)
                ? new BigDecimal(row[1].toString()).setScale(2, RoundingMode.HALF_UP)
                : BigDecimal.ZERO.setScale(2, RoundingMode.HALF_UP);

        summaryMap.put(branchCode, totalPL);
        
        // --- CALCULATION LOGIC ---
        totalAmount = totalAmount.add(totalPL);
    }

    // --- STEP 3: CONSTRUCT THE RESPONSE ---
    LhoSummaryResponseDto responseDto = LhoSummaryResponseDto.builder()
            .totalAmount(totalAmount.setScale(2, RoundingMode.HALF_UP))
            .totalRecordCount(summaryMap.size()) // Size of the map is the record count
            .circleWiseDetails(summaryMap)
            .build();

    // --- STEP 4: PERSIST ---
    try {
        String jsonPayload = objectMapper.writeValueAsString(responseDto);
        LhoTransferSummary summaryEntity = LhoTransferSummary.builder()
                .id(id)
                .payload(jsonPayload)
                .build();

        lhoSummaryRepository.save(summaryEntity);
        return responseDto;
    } catch (Exception e) {
        log.error("Failed to serialize summary: {}", e.getMessage());
        throw new RuntimeException("Error during LHO Summary persistence.");
    }
}

