Why this is the correct solution:
 * Single Pass Calculation: You are calculating the total amount while you are already looping through the data for the map. This is O(n) efficiency.
 * Metadata at the Top: Putting totalAmount and totalRecordCount at the root of the data object allows the frontend to display them in a "Header" or "Summary" section without having to loop through the details themselves.
 * Persistence: The LHO_TRANSFER_SUMMARY table will now store the totals as well, meaning you don't have to re-calculate them on a cache hit.
